{#
  Rendered by the vmagent role — do not edit on the box. Edit the Monitoring Agent (or Grove
  Settings) and hit Install.

  No targets are listed here and none are written to this box. Both jobs ask Grove what this
  agent scrapes; the labels (machine, region, server, and `engine` verbatim) arrive with each
  target, so nothing on this box has to be kept in step with the fleet.

  The SD token rides in the query string, not an Authorization header: Frappe's validate_auth
  rejects any header it cannot resolve to a user before the endpoint runs, so a bare shared
  secret cannot be sent that way. That puts a live credential in this file — hence its 0600 —
  and in Grove's own access log on every fetch.

  How often the lists are re-fetched is NOT here: vmagent rejects Prometheus's per-config
  `refresh_interval` on an http_sd_config and takes -promscrape.httpSDCheckInterval instead,
  set in the unit. Both jobs therefore share one interval.
#}
global:
  scrape_interval: {{ monitoring_scrape_interval }}

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: grove-host
    http_sd_configs:
      - url: "{{ monitoring_sd_url }}?agent={{ monitoring_agent | urlencode }}&kind=host&token={{ monitoring_sd_token | urlencode }}"

  - job_name: grove-engine
    scrape_interval: {{ monitoring_engine_scrape_interval }}
    http_sd_configs:
      - url: "{{ monitoring_sd_url }}?agent={{ monitoring_agent | urlencode }}&kind=engine&token={{ monitoring_sd_token | urlencode }}"
